    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The `ERROR GeneralExceptionHandler` line is from an existing negative-path test (UserRestControllerV1Tests), which passed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, region-validated `postcode` support for owners across the full OfficeFloor pipeline.\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema with pattern `^[0-9]{4}$`. Because it's not `required`, absent postcodes stay valid (backward-compatible), and since it's in `OwnerFields` it flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`), so it's stored and returned.\n\n**Persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 new `postcode` column + getter/setter.\n- Added a `postcode` column to all four DB schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). Tests run on hsqldb.\n\n**Validation (`ValidatePostcode.java`)** \u2014 a new function step that validates only when present: rejects non-4-digit values, and when the city maps to a known region enforces the fixed ranges (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode. Out-of-range \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400 via the existing `ValidationExceptionHandler`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 inserted the `validatePostcode` step (under the transaction governance) right after `validate` in both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`. On create, the postcode is persisted via the existing MapStruct `toOwner` mapping (name-matched, no change needed); for update I added `owner.setPostcode(...)` to `ApplyOwner`.\n\nThe three new acceptance tests (`coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode`) all pass, and the full suite (263 tests) remains green.",
